# {{ theme.name }} zsh-syntax-highlighting Theme

zsh-syntax-highlighting themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Requirements

- [zsh-syntax-highlighting](https://github.com/zsh-users/zsh-syntax-highlighting)

> [!WARNING]
> This theme must be loaded **after** zsh-syntax-highlighting.
> The theme works by overriding `ZSH_HIGHLIGHT_STYLES` variables set by zsh-syntax-highlighting.

## Installation

### Manual

Source the theme file in your `.zshrc`:

```bash
source /path/to/{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.zsh
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```bash
source /path/to/{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.zsh
```
{% endfor %}
